      "reasons": [
        "The claim that smooth movement includes “proper starting, stopping” is only indirectly supported in the packet (it discusses impaired initiation and inhibition in Parkinson’s disease, e.g., difficulty to start and stop walking), but the packet does not explicitly define smooth movement in terms of “proper starting, stopping.”",
        "The statement that “Better smooth movement is associated with faster, more controlled performance” is only partially supported: the packet reports correlation with “higher movement speed and increased smoothness of movement,” but it does not specifically mention “controlled performance.”"
